[{:db/id "q-320686/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "3ba4e6fa-0533-5f8f-9e17-ed9ac11a4680" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320686/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "23534205-d925-581b-819c-0b3a63a2bae8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320686/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f787ab61-7e81-5e51-9a54-ae6936d25143" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320686/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer-field/choices ["q-320686/field-1/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-320686/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320686/field-2/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "8446a18d-94ed-5b15-bd3c-ac795ed67864" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320686/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "d583b822-be47-50ee-bddf-8202fc4166d5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320686/field-2/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer-field/choices ["q-320686/field-2/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320686/field-3/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "58718824-7776-5b22-95a4-e86eb3885e29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320686/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b0eacc1-f9c6-5926-ab8f-4e60be0cefab" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320686/field-3/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer-field/choices ["q-320686/field-3/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320686" :question/id #uuid "814af89f-6240-5b38-a4c8-caac7366210d" :question/math-academy-id "q-320686" :question/problem "Find the points where the curve $x=4t,\\,y=\\frac{32}{t}$ intersects the line $\\frac{1}{2}x-y=0.$\n\nThe intersection points are $(-16,$\n{{field-1}}$)$ and $(${{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of intersection points, we take the equation of the line, replace $x$ and $y$ with the parametric formulas, and then solve for $t.$ Upon finding $t,$ we then find the coordinates of the intersection points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}x-y & =0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}(4t)-\\frac{32}{t} & =0 \\\\ 2t-\\frac{32}{t} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2{t}^{2}-32}{t} & =0 \\\\ 2{t}^{2}-32 & =0 \\\\ 2({t}^{2}-16) & =0 \\\\ 2(t+4)(t-4) & =0 \\\\ t & =\\pm 4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we have the values of $t,$ we proceed to find $x$ and $y.$ \n\n- We start with $t=-4.$ For $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4t \\\\  & =4(-4) \\\\  & =-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{32}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{(-4)} \\\\  & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coordinates of the first intersection point are $(-16,-8).$\n\n- We now move over to $t=4.$ For $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4t \\\\  & =4(4) \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{32}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{4} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coordinates of the second intersection point are $(16,8).$\n\nTherefore, the curve $x=4t,\\,y=\\frac{32}{t}$ intersects the line $\\frac{1}{2}x-y=0$ at the points $(-16,-8)$ and $(16,8).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320686/field-1" "q-320686/field-2" "q-320686/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afc21191-a71b-5dac-8a4a-e46e8bc03a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320686"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274671/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "435ff245-ff47-5939-ae21-4ea4d0a92b25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274671/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ab80bea9-201d-5742-aad6-fc6eeeb9bfc7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274671/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer-field/choices ["q-274671/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274671/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "e9297d38-5550-5b27-9cfb-335af5980727" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274671/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "24a0e711-94c0-58a4-a8ce-787bad8b43a7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274671/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-274671/field-2/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274671" :question/id #uuid "1a1e3d7b-489e-57fd-97e8-34f13b4e5257" :question/math-academy-id "q-274671" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14061747/assets/3ec88af84d96caed2c27b9b1596b5320ff7ceaaac71ce12e48623c2be52f18ba.png)\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $t$ at which the curve $x=t+6,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-4$ intersects the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-1$ (shown above) are\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}$,\\,t=$\n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the line and curve intersect twice, so we expect two solutions.\n\nTo find the coordinates of the intersection points, we take the equation of the line, replace $x$ and $y$ with the parametric formulas, and then solve for $t.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}x-1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-4 & =\\frac{1}{2}(t+6)-1 \\\\ {t}^{2}-8 & =(t+6)-2 \\\\ {t}^{2}-8 & =t+4 \\\\ {t}^{2}-t-12 & =0 \\\\ (t+3)(t-4) & =0 \\\\ t & =-3,\\,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the values of $t$ where the curve $x=t+6,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-4$ intersects the line $y=\\frac{1}{2}x-1$ are $t=-3$ and $t=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-274671/field-1" "q-274671/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afc21191-a71b-5dac-8a4a-e46e8bc03a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-274673/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "e97f438d-0294-501a-8248-3306ad8af745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274673/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "2c57436f-bc5d-502c-96e6-6d12543d5e8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274673/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6cddf78a-4b10-581b-b222-be57730f9a28" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274673/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer-field/choices ["q-274673/field-1/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-274673/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274673/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "c41ba5df-2a19-532e-91b7-78663ce57225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274673/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "eceeb209-5315-5811-bdba-28b78081f09b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274673/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer-field/choices ["q-274673/field-2/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274673/field-3/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "578388b3-345b-582e-b356-ee5c92988fcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-274673/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "cb5bb6f7-0379-5573-9ff2-8bec978d727c" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-274673/field-3/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer-field/choices ["q-274673/field-3/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-274673" :question/id #uuid "dbb7e394-0cf1-5a5c-a310-9a9d31edc44a" :question/math-academy-id "q-274673" :question/problem "Find the points where the curve $x={t}^{2},\\,y=4t$ intersects the line $x+y+3=0.$\n\nThe intersection points are $(1,$\n{{field-1}}$)$ and $(${{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}$).$" :question/worked-solution "To find the coordinates of intersection points, we take the equation of the line, replace $x$ and $y$ with the parametric formulas, and then solve for $t.$ Upon finding $t,$ we then find the coordinates of the intersection points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+y+3 & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}+4t+3 & =0 \\\\ (t+3)(t+1) & =0 \\\\ t & =-3,-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we have the values of $t,$ we proceed to find $x$ and $y:$ \n\n- We start with $t=-3.$ For $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2} \\\\  & =(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4t \\\\  & =4(-3) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coordinates of the first intersection point are $(9,-12).$\n\n- We now move over to $t=-1.$ For $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={t}^{2} \\\\  & =(-1)^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4t \\\\  & =4(-1) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coordinates of the second intersection point are $(1,-4).$\n\nTherefore, the curve $x={t}^{2},y=4t$ intersects the line $x+y+3=0$ at the points $(1,-4)$ and $(9,-12).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-274673/field-1" "q-274673/field-2" "q-274673/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "afc21191-a71b-5dac-8a4a-e46e8bc03a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-274673"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16166/selection/05c13ac9d943c3a5ae32e1f2b177eff9d5ce5143f22a7899cbc542e946718e73" :answer/id #uuid "198441e9-2ce9-5e01-8be8-414085342ac1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-\\frac{1}{2},3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16166/selection/76891132f99087c955421da80afb724f9134dcc8d960151d483057247e2d560e" :answer/id #uuid "adc2d09d-0547-50d5-a512-65d1bdabff44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-\\frac{1}{2},4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16166/selection/dd7ac70017064fd639d8c6fc7749ec2a4de11fa51420cf3b819d4e2fe2e4cf8a" :answer/id #uuid "73cdaf68-24f2-5188-8dee-bc4ae5ecd42b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-1,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16166/selection/5dec233d3ad7cfae0cedb480becaeb84a2ae4e1a32c08bbf7f24d0264c31963c" :answer/id #uuid "428faf37-52e0-523b-8347-6fa422602042" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t=-1,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16166/selection/cd9b9f4018a5ef53d0aa05cfeb5fe138c4e58e23e5fbe5e4e